 "notes": "Printed page 260; it repeats the Table XV Part II (B) header. On this page the subsidiary headers are printed 'Dogri.', 'Panjabi.', 'Kashmiri.' without the (B)/(C)/(D) letters. Same 12 figure columns + Remarks. The whole page is inside the 'KASHMIR SOUTH' brace (= Part I 'Kashmir South (including Municipality)'), continued from leaf 269. Blocks: 'Awantipura Tehsil' (10 rows: Chabhali, Pothwari, Shina all nil); a tehsil printed as 'Khas Tehsil' over a rule with 'Srinagar Tehsil' beneath, recorded as 'Khas Tehsil (Srinagar Tehsil)' (10 rows: Chabhali, Pothwari, Ladakhi, Shina all nil); 'Srinagar Municipality' (Dogri and Kashmiri on this leaf, block continues on leaf 271). DISCREPANCY: Awantipura Panjabi, Dogri subsidiary is printed Persons 45, Males 54, Females nil. The print is clear under a tight zoom, but persons < males is impossible; Kashmiri shows 54/54 and the remark says '54 males speak 3 languages', so 45 is almost certainly transposed digits for 54. Recorded as printed (45). Khas/Srinagar Tehsil Panjabi males: the middle digit is broken type, read as 4 (a 4 missing its diagonal; not a 1). 348 + 229 = 577 confirms it. Other remarks agree with the figures. Cross-check with Part II(A): leaf0260.json has Awantipura Dogri subsidiary Punjabi 3/-/3, but Part B prints 8/7/1. leaf0261.json has Srinagar Municipality Kashmiri subsidiary Punjabi -/-/98 (males nil), but Part B prints 1/1/- . Part B exceeds Part A in both; left as printed."
}